(* Spec: lane vortex-chain-20261111-142342, rung C2 (SPEC-C2, Claude Opus 5.5, 2026-11-11; drafted from 17:50 EST, times from date). Vortex Echo purist module tasks/bubble-echo/vortex/purist/vortex_a1.wasm (sha256 a3cf8c82) on its exact bytes, under wasmc (wasm plus frame-free direct calls), pop path only (the 520 pop ticks after the puncture, and the end of the pop). This is the v1 pop, not the v5.8 pop. Pure HOL over PROVED theorems restated verbatim below; no new stepping of the bytes:
   from pop_r5_r4c.spec (sha256 9b8aab73, FROZEN-R4C.txt): VA1_TICK_FORWARD_POP_R5C (one forward pop tick, with NO routine-contract premise: droplet birth is discharged there by VA1_BIRTH_OK, so no theorem here carries va1_birth_ok; this folds the ladder's rung C2c into C2), VA1_TICK_POP_INVERSE_R5 (one backward pop tick undoes a forward one, for every births list L the forward contract allows), VA1_LOG_OK_POP_FWD, VA1_ST_SAT; from pop_design_r0_end.spec (sha256 a58767df): VA1_TICK_FORWARD_POP_END (R0: once the clock has reached P + 520, tick_forward returns 0 and changes no memory); from chain_c1_final.spec (sha256 3b62701f, FROZEN-C1.txt): the generic host-call layer va1_hcall, va1_hrun, va1_cmds_ok, va1_cmds_end exactly as pinned there, with its generic theorems. Every copied entry is byte-identical to its frozen source (checked by tools/gen_c2.py).
   Host-call model (C1's, unchanged): va1_hcall step code args r Q gl m says that the export body has an entry offset and declared-local values computed from its own bytes, and that from EVERY state with memory size 4194304, globals gl and memory m, the module-entry state (wcall_entry: params plus zeroed declared locals, empty stack and labels, arity 1) reaches under step, on every path and without getting stuck, status WDone with result stack [I32 r], memory size 4194304 and Q of its globals and memory. va1_hrun step cs Q runs a list of tick commands (T = tick_forward, F = tick_backward), each as one host call that returns 1, on the globals and memory the previous call left. Assumed, as in WebAssembly and not proved: between calls the host writes neither memory nor globals, and memory does not grow.
   History invariant (new): S ranges over the 8-tuples (ra,rb,jq,jp,di,zq,zp,nd) that va1_st takes (rim rings ra/rb, wobble rings jq/jp, droplet words di, ripple rings zq/zp, droplet count nd); va1_diof / va1_ndof project di and nd. va1_pop_reach mdl hp tbl p t0 S0 u S says S is the end of a legal forward history of u pop ticks from S0 with the clock starting at t0: each step applies va1_pop_fwd va1_ck va1_jigk L with SOME births list L that the forward contract allows (every born record has word 6 = the new clock and words 10, 11 = 0, and the count stays <= 16384). The births contract does not pin which droplets are born, so neither does this: after a rewind, running forward again is not proved to repeat the same births. va1_pop_at mdl N p ap x0 hp tbl t0 S0 u m says memory m is a pop state at step u: va1_st with clock word (val t0 + u), pop word p, auto-pop word ap, model mdl, the 3N vortex words in use = u swirl steps of x0 (one ve_fredkin_fwd (ve_vk mdl) per pop tick), header words hp, speed table tbl, and pop data S for SOME S in the reach set. At u = 0 the reach set is exactly {S0}.
   Headlines. VA1_POP_SCRUB: inside the pop window (P set, val p <= val t0, val t0 + K <= val p + 520, val p + 520 < 2^32 so the clock never wraps) and from a start state whose droplet log is well formed (va1_log_ok: count <= 16384, every droplet's birth tick <= t0, unused droplet words 0), any command list that keeps the step in [0, K] runs with every call returning 1, the globals unchanged, and ends in a pop state at the end step. VA1_POP_CHAIN_INVERSE: k forward calls then k backward calls restore everything va1_st pins (clock, pop word, auto-pop word, model, the 3N vortex words in use, header, speed table, all four rings, both ripple rings, every droplet word and the droplet count). VA1_POP_CHAIN_TO_END: from the first pop tick (t0 = p), 520 forward calls each return 1; then one more forward call returns 0 and leaves globals and memory unchanged; then 520 backward calls each return 1 and restore everything va1_st pins. VA1_POP_CHAIN_SAT: every abstract state is realised by some memory, and one instance satisfies all the hypotheses of VA1_POP_CHAIN_TO_END at once (so of VA1_POP_SCRUB with K = 520, u = 0 and of VA1_POP_CHAIN_INVERSE with t0 = p). VA1_POP_SCRUB_FRAME / VA1_POP_CHAIN_BYTES: additionally every byte of the 4 MiB memory outside the clock word [16392,16396), the droplet-count word [16400,16404) and [1114112,2039808) (vortex arrays, rings, droplet arrays and the scratch area) is unchanged byte for byte. Read together with va1_st this means that at the end of VA1_POP_CHAIN_BYTES every byte is as it was except the scratch area [1966080,2039808) and the unused vortex words VA/VB[3N..2048); that reading is an immediate consequence, not itself a theorem of this spec, and those two areas do differ in raw-memory tests. Never read as "every byte" or "identical memory".
   Not covered: the puncture tick that starts the pop and its undo (later rungs), the no-pop film (C1), which droplets are born, and the page's GPU tracers (outside the module). The start conditions are what the real post-puncture states are TESTED (chain scout, 1,765 real pop snapshots), not proved, to satisfy. Proved in Hearth's model of WebAssembly.
   Recursive constants (va1_pop_reach, and the copied va1_cmds_ok, va1_cmds_end, ve_isq, ve_vk_rs, ve_vk_acc, wdecl_vals, va1_push, ve_kd_fwdn) are pinned by their CLAUSES theorems (va1_hrun is a pinned ITLIST definition; VA1_HRUN_CLAUSES is its unfolding); every other constant the statements reach is pinned by a definition entry. Prove with plain --spec, not --benchmark (as for chain_c1_final.spec). *)

(* ---- C2 definitions ---- *)
definition va1_fs_pop
 `va1_fs_pop (fs:num->byte list#num#num) <=>
    fs 9 = (va1_f9_mc,0,0) /\ fs 10 = (va1_f10_mc,0,0) /\ fs 11 = (va1_f11_mc,0,0) /\
    fs 12 = (va1_f12_mc,0,0) /\ fs 13 = (va1_f13_mc,0,1) /\ fs 14 = (va1_f14_mc,0,1) /\
    fs 15 = (va1_f15_mc,0,0) /\ fs 16 = (va1_f16_mc,0,0) /\ fs 17 = (va1_f17_mc,1,0) /\
    fs 18 = (va1_f18_mc,1,0) /\ fs 19 = (va1_f19_mc,0,0) /\ fs 20 = (va1_f20_mc,0,0) /\
    fs 21 = (va1_f21_mc,0,0) /\ fs 22 = (va1_f22_mc,0,0) /\ fs 23 = (va1_f23_mc,0,0) /\
    fs 24 = (va1_f24_mc,0,0) /\ fs 27 = (va1_f27_mc,0,0) /\ fs 28 = (va1_f28_mc,0,0)`;;
definition va1_diof
 `va1_diof (S:(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#int32) =
    FST(SND(SND(SND(SND S))))`;;
definition va1_ndof
 `va1_ndof (S:(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#int32) =
    SND(SND(SND(SND(SND(SND(SND S))))))`;;
allow va1_pop_reach;;
theorem VA1_POP_REACH_CLAUSES
 `(!(mdl:num->int32) (hp:num->int32) (tbl:num->int32) (p:int32) (t0:int32)
    (S0:(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#int32) S.
     va1_pop_reach mdl hp tbl p t0 S0 0 S <=> S = S0) /\
  (!(mdl:num->int32) (hp:num->int32) (tbl:num->int32) (p:int32) (t0:int32)
    (S0:(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#int32) u S.
     va1_pop_reach mdl hp tbl p t0 S0 (SUC u) S <=>
     ?S' (L:(num->int32)list).
        va1_pop_reach mdl hp tbl p t0 S0 u S' /\
        ALL (\r. r 6 = word (val t0 + u + 1) /\ r 10 = word 0 /\ r 11 = word 0) L /\
        val (va1_ndof S') + LENGTH L <= 16384 /\
        S = va1_pop_fwd va1_ck va1_jigk L mdl hp tbl (word (val t0 + u)) p S')`;;
definition va1_pop_at
 `va1_pop_at (mdl:num->int32) (N:num) (p:int32) (ap:int32) (x0:(num->int32)#(num->int32))
             (hp:num->int32) (tbl:num->int32) (t0:int32)
             (S0:(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#int32)
             (u:num) (m:int64->byte) <=>
    ?S. va1_pop_reach mdl hp tbl p t0 S0 u S /\
        va1_st (word (val t0 + u)) p ap mdl N (ITER u (ve_fredkin_fwd (ve_vk mdl)) x0) hp tbl S m`;;
definition va1_pop_frame
 `va1_pop_frame (m0:int64->byte) (m:int64->byte) <=>
    !a. a < 4194304 /\ ~(16392 <= a /\ a < 16396) /\ ~(16400 <= a /\ a < 16404) /\
        ~(1114112 <= a /\ a < 2039808)
        ==> read (bytes8 (word a)) m = read (bytes8 (word a)) m0`;;

(* ---- C2: one host call per pop tick ---- *)
theorem VA1_POP_HCALL_FWD
 `!(fs:num->byte list#num#num) (gl:num->wval) (t:int32) (p:int32) (ap:int32) (mdl:num->int32) (N:num)
   (x:(num->int32)#(num->int32)) (hp:num->int32) (tbl:num->int32)
   (S:(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#int32)
   (m:int64->byte).
     mdl 1 = word N /\ 1 <= N /\ N <= 640 /\ va1_fs_pop fs /\
     va1_pop_window t p /\ va1_log_ok t (va1_diof S) (va1_ndof S) /\
     va1_st t p ap mdl N x hp tbl S m
     ==> va1_hcall (wasmc fs) va1_tick_forward_mc [] (word 1)
           (\gl' m'. gl' = gl /\
              ?L. ALL (\r. r 6 = word_add t (word 1) /\ r 10 = word 0 /\ r 11 = word 0) L /\
                  val (va1_ndof S) + LENGTH L <= 16384 /\
                  va1_st (word_add t (word 1)) p ap mdl N (ve_fredkin_fwd (ve_vk mdl) x) hp tbl
                         (va1_pop_fwd va1_ck va1_jigk L mdl hp tbl t p S) m') gl m`;;
theorem VA1_POP_HCALL_BWD
 `!(fs:num->byte list#num#num) (gl:num->wval) (t:int32) (p:int32) (ap:int32) (mdl:num->int32) (N:num)
   (x:(num->int32)#(num->int32)) (hp:num->int32) (tbl:num->int32)
   (S:(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#int32)
   (L:(num->int32)list) (m:int64->byte).
     mdl 1 = word N /\ 1 <= N /\ N <= 640 /\ va1_fs_pop fs /\
     va1_pop_window t p /\ va1_log_ok t (va1_diof S) (va1_ndof S) /\
     ALL (\r. r 6 = word_add t (word 1)) L /\ val (va1_ndof S) + LENGTH L <= 16384 /\
     va1_st (word_add t (word 1)) p ap mdl N (ve_fredkin_fwd (ve_vk mdl) x) hp tbl
            (va1_pop_fwd va1_ck va1_jigk L mdl hp tbl t p S) m
     ==> va1_hcall (wasmc fs) va1_tick_backward_mc [] (word 1)
           (\gl' m'. gl' = gl /\ va1_st t p ap mdl N x hp tbl S m') gl m`;;
theorem VA1_POP_HCALL_END
 `!(fs:num->byte list#num#num) (gl:num->wval) (t:int32) (p:int32) (ap:int32) (m:int64->byte).
     ~(p = word 4294967295) /\ val p <= val t /\ val (word_add p (word 520)) <= val t /\
     va1_tick t m /\ va1_pop p ap m
     ==> va1_hcall (wasmc fs) va1_tick_forward_mc [] (word 0) (\gl' m'. gl' = gl /\ m' = m) gl m`;;

(* ---- C2: the history invariant ---- *)
theorem VA1_POP_REACH_LOG_OK
 `!(mdl:num->int32) (hp:num->int32) (tbl:num->int32) (p:int32) (t0:int32)
   (S0:(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#int32)
   (u:num)
   (S:(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#int32).
     va1_log_ok t0 (va1_diof S0) (va1_ndof S0) /\ val t0 + u < 4294967296 /\
     va1_pop_reach mdl hp tbl p t0 S0 u S
     ==> va1_log_ok (word (val t0 + u)) (va1_diof S) (va1_ndof S)`;;

(* ---- C2 headlines: scrub in any order, the inverse chain, the end of the pop, non-vacuity ---- *)
theorem VA1_POP_SCRUB
 `!(fs:num->byte list#num#num) (gl:num->wval) (mdl:num->int32) (N:num) (p:int32) (ap:int32)
   (x0:(num->int32)#(num->int32)) (hp:num->int32) (tbl:num->int32) (t0:int32)
   (S0:(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#int32)
   (K:num).
     mdl 1 = word N /\ 1 <= N /\ N <= 640 /\ va1_fs_pop fs /\
     ~(p = word 4294967295) /\ val p <= val t0 /\ val t0 + K <= val p + 520 /\ val p + 520 < 4294967296 /\
     va1_log_ok t0 (va1_diof S0) (va1_ndof S0)
     ==> !(cs:bool list) (u:num) (m:int64->byte).
           u <= K /\ va1_cmds_ok K u cs /\ va1_pop_at mdl N p ap x0 hp tbl t0 S0 u m
           ==> va1_hrun (wasmc fs) cs
                 (\gl' m'. gl' = gl /\
                    va1_pop_at mdl N p ap x0 hp tbl t0 S0 (va1_cmds_end u cs) m') gl m`;;
theorem VA1_POP_CHAIN_INVERSE
 `!(fs:num->byte list#num#num) (gl:num->wval) (mdl:num->int32) (N:num) (p:int32) (ap:int32)
   (x0:(num->int32)#(num->int32)) (hp:num->int32) (tbl:num->int32) (t0:int32)
   (S0:(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#int32)
   (k:num) (m:int64->byte).
     mdl 1 = word N /\ 1 <= N /\ N <= 640 /\ va1_fs_pop fs /\
     ~(p = word 4294967295) /\ val p <= val t0 /\ val t0 + k <= val p + 520 /\ val p + 520 < 4294967296 /\
     va1_log_ok t0 (va1_diof S0) (va1_ndof S0) /\ va1_st t0 p ap mdl N x0 hp tbl S0 m
     ==> va1_hrun (wasmc fs) (APPEND (REPLICATE k T) (REPLICATE k F))
           (\gl' m'. gl' = gl /\ va1_st t0 p ap mdl N x0 hp tbl S0 m') gl m`;;
theorem VA1_POP_CHAIN_TO_END
 `!(fs:num->byte list#num#num) (gl:num->wval) (mdl:num->int32) (N:num) (p:int32) (ap:int32)
   (x0:(num->int32)#(num->int32)) (hp:num->int32) (tbl:num->int32)
   (S0:(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#int32)
   (m:int64->byte).
     mdl 1 = word N /\ 1 <= N /\ N <= 640 /\ va1_fs_pop fs /\
     ~(p = word 4294967295) /\ val p + 520 < 4294967296 /\
     va1_log_ok p (va1_diof S0) (va1_ndof S0) /\ va1_st p p ap mdl N x0 hp tbl S0 m
     ==> va1_hrun (wasmc fs) (REPLICATE 520 T)
           (\gl1 m1. gl1 = gl /\ va1_pop_at mdl N p ap x0 hp tbl p S0 520 m1 /\
              va1_hcall (wasmc fs) va1_tick_forward_mc [] (word 0)
                (\gl2 m2. gl2 = gl1 /\ m2 = m1 /\
                   va1_hrun (wasmc fs) (REPLICATE 520 F)
                     (\gl3 m3. gl3 = gl /\ va1_st p p ap mdl N x0 hp tbl S0 m3) gl2 m2) gl1 m1) gl m`;;
theorem VA1_POP_CHAIN_SAT
 `(!(t:int32) (p:int32) (ap:int32) (mdl:num->int32) (N:num) (x:(num->int32)#(num->int32))
    (hp:num->int32) (tbl:num->int32)
    (S:(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#int32).
     N <= 640 ==> ?m:int64->byte. va1_st t p ap mdl N x hp tbl S m) /\
  (?(fs:num->byte list#num#num) (mdl:num->int32) (N:num) (p:int32) (ap:int32)
    (x0:(num->int32)#(num->int32)) (hp:num->int32) (tbl:num->int32)
    (S0:(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#int32)
    (m:int64->byte).
     mdl 1 = word N /\ 1 <= N /\ N <= 640 /\ va1_fs_pop fs /\
     ~(p = word 4294967295) /\ val p + 520 < 4294967296 /\
     va1_log_ok p (va1_diof S0) (va1_ndof S0) /\ va1_st p p ap mdl N x0 hp tbl S0 m)`;;

(* ---- C2 byte frame ---- *)
theorem VA1_POP_SCRUB_FRAME
 `!(fs:num->byte list#num#num) (gl:num->wval) (mdl:num->int32) (N:num) (p:int32) (ap:int32)
   (x0:(num->int32)#(num->int32)) (hp:num->int32) (tbl:num->int32) (t0:int32)
   (S0:(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#(num->int32)#int32)
   (K:num).
     mdl 1 = word N /\ 1 <= N /\ N <= 640 /\ va1_fs_pop fs /\
     ~(p = word 4294967295) /\ val p <= val t0 /\ val t0 + K <= val p + 520 /\ val p + 520 < 4294967296 /\
     va1_log_ok t0 (va1_diof S0) (va1_ndof S0)
     ==> !(cs:bool list) (u:num) (m:int64->byte).
